# Force LF line endings for text files on all platforms.
#
# Without this, Windows git's default autocrlf=true converts text-file
# line endings to CRLF on checkout. Several test suites read embedded
# .md / .yaml prompts and assert on substrings anchored on "\n" (e.g.
# the agent-prompt frontmatter tests in internal/scaffold/agents/ and
# the playbook tests in internal/scaffold/plans/). CRLF breaks every
# such anchor on Windows. Forcing LF universally keeps the source tree
# byte-identical across platforms, so the same string assertions work.

# Markdown — canonical agent prompts, playbooks, decision journal, etc.
*.md          text eol=lf

# YAML — agents.yaml, models.yaml, agents-default.yaml, GitHub workflows.
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf

# TOML — Codex hook fragments, agent definitions.
*.toml        text eol=lf

# JSON — Gemini hook fragments, manifest, spec graph nodes.
*.json        text eol=lf

# Go source — defensive; Go tooling tolerates CRLF but tests that read
# Go source as bytes (rare but possible) would break the same way.
*.go          text eol=lf

# Shell scripts — CRLF would prevent them from running.
*.sh          text eol=lf

# Default: let git detect text vs binary, normalize text to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
